      "final_text": "我们的观点：零售销售数据走软，与近期通胀压力趋缓的背景相符，但即便以实际值衡量，核心零售支出增长依然疲弱。我们此前已预期消费者前景将有所走弱，尤其是考虑到今年上半年若干异常因素对消费增长的提振效应，以及这些因素在下半年将逐步消退。这些因素包括：退税刺激效应、世界杯对消费的拉动，以及亚马逊将Prime Day从往常的Q3提前至今年Q2。展望后市，驱动消费者支出的将主要是基本面收入因素——而这些驱动因素目前仍然疲软。美国消费者仍面临工资增长滞后于通胀压力的困境。通胀冲击正在侵蚀实际收入，并将储蓄率压低至2.8%（为2000年代中期以来的最低水平）。美国经济增长温和，且集中于人工智能(AI)相关板块，目前尚未出现明显的生产率提升效果。美联储加息已提上日程，这也对宏观背景构成挑战。上周消费者价格指数(CPI)及生产者价格指数(PPI)数据符合预期或略低于预期，叠加零售销售数据走软，已将美联储在9月联邦公开市场委员会(FOMC)会议上加息的概率降至约30%。总体而言，我们认为宏观前景面临的下行风险大于上行空间。",
      "iterations": 1,
      "seg_status": "machine",
      "source_text": "What we think The softer retail sales data makes sense in the context of lower near-term inflationary pressures, but even in real terms, core retail spending growth has been weak. We have been expecting a weaker consumer picture, especially due to the unusual factors boosting consumer growth in the first half of this year and how these factors would fade in the second half. Those factors are: the tax refund stimulus, the World Cup boost to consumption, and Amazon shifting Prime Day from the usual Q3 to Q2 this year. From here, it is mainly fundamental income drivers that would power consumer spending going forward—and these drivers remain soft. The U.S. consumer is still dealing with wage growth that has lagged inflationary pressures. Inflation shocks are eroding real incomes and pushing the saving rate to 2.8% (lowest since the mid-2000s). U.S. growth is moderate but concentrated in AI-related sectors, with no evident productivity payoff yet. Fed hikes are now in play, which also challenges the macro backdrop. The in-line to softer CPI and PPI prints last week, coupled with soft retail sales data, have reduced the probabilities for a Fed hike at the September FOMC meeting to around 30%. Overall, we see more downside than upside risks to our macro outlook.",
